+## 2026-08-18 — A6 burned-seed pilot passed; `a6_a4` selected for holdout
+
+**Evidence accepted**: the canonical arm-selection artifact is
+`result/a6_pilot/20260819T005514Z/SELECTION.json`, generated from the
+24-cell burned-seed pilot by the verified selection code at
+`c663fcf5b7a142db595738c8b20bb83549f1ab99`. The audit found exactly 24
+complete, sane, certified checkpoints (12 per arm), no budget exhaustion,
+all recorded solves OPTIMAL, and all replay, completeness, trigger-stream,
+and certification gates passing.
+
+**Prespecified selection rule and result**: `a6_a3` would advance only if
+it achieved a strictly lower total-call score than `a6_a4` on at least
+9/12 matched pilot instances, with ties counted as non-wins. It won 2/12;
+`a6_a4` won the other 10 with no ties. Because every cell certified, each
+score is its calls to certificate. Median scores were 23 for `a6_a4`
+(range 13--31) and 32.5 for `a6_a3` (range 21--60).
+
+**Decision**: freeze `a6_a4` as the sole A6 arm for the holdout. The pilot
+is an implementation and arm-selection gate only: seeds 0--15 remain
+burned and these results are not evaluation evidence that A6 beats A2.
+No constants, triggers, recovery rules, budgets, or acceptance thresholds
+change after observing the pilot.
+
+**Next gate**: after this artifact and decision entry are committed, build
+the already-prespecified holdout pipeline for exactly 128 method-cells:
+A2 plus `a6_a4` on seeds 16--31 x n in {8, 12} x b in {0.01, 0.05}.
+No other method, seed, scale, or damping experiment is authorized by this
+decision.
